worker_module_budget
  module "formal_ai_worker_facts_and_software_phrases.js"
  ceiling 1307
  rationale 'Fact questions resolved through the fact cache, Wikidata and Wiktionary, and the software artifact and object-phrase scanner. Issue #658 cut this module out of one oversized worker file by line count; R1188-U5 named it after what it holds. Its ceiling falls as its logic moves into js/wasm-worker. Ceiling moved 1151 to 1389 with issue #1175''s object-phrase twin (objectPhraseArtifact and its boundary/lead tables mirroring object_phrase_artifact in src/solver_handlers/software_project.rs): the artifact kind is read only from the head noun of the authoring verb''s object phrase, so a regex request mentioning a ZIP-code "extension" is not an extension project. Ceiling moved 1388 to 1290 for issue #1172 R3, because the hardcoded FACT_RESPONSE_TEMPLATES table, renderFactSummary and wikipediaSitelinkUrl left for the seeded fact_live_answer template that factLiveSummary renders in formal_ai_worker_factual_qa.js. Ceiling moved 1290 to 1292 (R1188-U5): the first comment lines say what the module holds. Issue #1580 records the existing main worker at exactly 1307 lines (15 more than the stale 1292 ceiling). The merged live-Wikidata changes preserve captured URL/SHA evidence, reject ambiguous subject matches, support localized subject spellings and claim values, and honor offline and service preferences. This PR adds no worker logic here: the complete module is byte-identical to main aa93fe9c. Only this measured module ceiling changes; the 3000-line total target and every other module ceiling remain in force.'
